- op: discuss  # 2513
  at: '2026-09-16T16:32:32Z'  # 2513
  by: agent  # 2513
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2513
  clock: 17  # 2513
  nonce: '2513'  # 2513
  message: "RE-POINTED, NOT CLOSED. Status stays violated. 2026-09-16 at dev 9c8c8165f0.\n\nThis is a STANDING parity invariant, and its own 2026-03-03 entry says so:\n\"will re-violate if future bakeoffs find new gaps\". So the question at re-verify\ntime is not \"did the old gaps close\" but \"is there a gap NOW\". Both halves\nanswered below.\n\n1. THE CITED EVIDENCE HAS DRAINED. The 2026-06-08 re-violation rested on two\nitems, and both closed under their own names without this row updating:\n\n  INV-loguk (non-Python analyzers do not populate cyclomatic_complexity) -\n  SATISFIED. Filed as \"bash callables get cyclomatic_complexity 0/2 vs\n  java/go/rust/swift/csharp/ts 100%\". Re-measured on the self-analysis corpus:\n  bash is 13/13, 100%.\n\n  INV-golap (JS populates signature on 0/10 function|method nodes vs TS 25/26) -\n  SATISFIED. Filed here as \"JS sig 2/5\". Re-measured: 17/18 (94.4%) on the\n  self-analysis corpus, and 5/5 vs 5/5 on matched js/ts fixtures under\n  META-rozur, which closed satisfied today on that evidence.\n\nPer-language populate rates, function|method nodes, self-analysis corpus:\n\n  language     cyclomatic_complexity   signature\n  python       32782/32795  100.0%     32782/32795  100.0%\n  typescript      40/42      95.2%         42/42     100.0%\n  javascript      16/18      88.9%         17/18      94.4%\n  bash            13/13     100.0%         13/13     100.0%\n  go              10/12      83.3%          8/12      66.7%\n  java             6/6      100.0%          6/6      100.0%\n  csharp           5/5      100.0%          5/5      100.0%\n  rust             5/7       71.4%          7/7      100.0%\n  swift            4/7       57.1%          6/7       85.7%\n  elixir           0/2        0.0%          0/2        0.0%\n  php              0/2        0.0%          0/2        0.0%\n\n2. A LIVE GAP REPLACES IT, AND IT IS THIS INVARIANT'S EXACT SHAPE. The\nroot_cause field reads: \"Features are developed for one language and not\nscope-expanded to closely related languages that share the same AST patterns\nand programming idioms.\" That is a literal description of the package-level\ncall-anchor fix:\n\n  Go received it. A call inside a package-level function literal emitted no\n  calls edge; the fix anchors on the module-level declaration's own symbol,\n  else the file pseudo-symbol, with both scope walks sharing one helper.\n  Measured before the fix at 578 of 1331 fmt.Fprintf sites invisible on one\n  repo (43.4%). Shipped in PR #746.\n\n  Nine sibling tree-sitter analyzers did not, and each fails at the same place -\n  the enclosing-scope walk returns None at the file root. Fixture-proven with a\n  positive control per language: rust, java, kotlin, swift, ruby, c, cpp, scala,\n  lua all emit NOTHING at the package-level site while emitting normally at the\n  in-named-function control. csharp additionally drops every unresolved callee.\n  js, ts, py and php already anchor, which is what makes this a parity gap\n  rather than a universal limitation.\n\n  Evidence lives at ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/nopoh_pkglit_09032026/sweep/\n  (fixtures + runner, one source file per language, three sites each). Filed as\n  INV-bamij; cited here as evidence, and the sweep artifacts are the durable\n  pointer if that row closes.\n\n3. NOT LOAD-BEARING, RECORDED SO IT IS NOT LOST: elixir and php sit at 0/2 on\nboth metrics above. n=2 on a Python-dominant corpus is too thin to file as a\nparity violation - hypergumbo's own tree has almost no elixir or php. Confirm\non a corpus with real elixir/php volume before treating it as evidence.\n\nRE-VERIFY TRIGGER, since a standing invariant with no trigger is how this row\nwent three months pointing at closed items: re-run section 2 when INV-bamij\nresolves, and re-run section 1's table after any analyzer-metadata sweep. If\nboth come back clean, this row is satisfiable - on positive evidence, not on\nthe absence of a filed instance."  # 2513
